{"name":"Sour Face","hex":"#adc979","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of acidity.","Made rancid by fermentation, etc."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sensation of a sour taste.","A drink made with whiskey, lemon or lime juice and sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour"},{"term":"face","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The front part of the head of a human or other animal, featuring the eyes, nose, and mouth, and the surrounding area.","One's facial expression."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To position oneself or itself so as to have one's face closest to (something).","To have its front closest to, or in the direction of (something else)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/face"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ben Myers","blocks":[{"text":"Benjamin Myers FRSL is an English writer, novelist, and journalist."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Myers"},{"title":"Sourness","blocks":[{"text":"Sourness, also known as sour, is a basic taste sensation perceived through hydrogen ions from acidic compounds interacting with taste bud receptors, and it can also refer to an unpleasant or acidic quality in taste, disposition, or tone. It is a warning sign for potentially spoiled food, though it is balanced in some food products by sweetness, and it is associated with a low pH."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lemon_with_white_background.jpg/330px-Lemon_with_white_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sourness"},{"title":"Face","blocks":[{"text":"The face is \"the front part of the head of a human or other animal, featuring the eyes, nose and mouth, and the surrounding area.\" While that basic structure is found in many animals, the evolutionary development of mammals has led to a wide diversity of facial types between those species, identifiable by characteristics of facial features and expressive behaviors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Human_faces.jpg/330px-Human_faces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Face"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Essig-1.jpg/500px-Essig-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Essig-1.jpg/1280px-Essig-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Essig-1.jpg/500px-Essig-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEssig-1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Joghurt.jpg/500px-Joghurt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Joghurt.jpg/1280px-Joghurt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Joghurt.jpg/500px-Joghurt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoghurt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Sobo_1909_260.png/500px-Sobo_1909_260.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Sobo_1909_260.png/1280px-Sobo_1909_260.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Sobo_1909_260.png/500px-Sobo_1909_260.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt"